    "rules": [
      "Do not use one generic temperature for all glass manufacturing.",
      "Do not use downstream glass-processing temperature as the furnace melting temperature.",
      "Do not apply heat pumps to primary glass melting.",
      "Do not assume electric melting is feasible for every glass plant.",
      "Do not assume the national coal/pet coke mix applies to every plant.",
      "Use furnace-specific measured data whenever available.",
      "Use BEE case-study savings as reference values, not guaranteed project savings.",
      "Cullet availability and quality must be explicit inputs.",
      "Check electrical infrastructure before recommending electric boosting or electric melting.",
      "Treat continuous furnace operation and reliability as hard constraints."
